gov/how-do-you-measure-it/how-do-you-measure-flammability", "images": [{"height": 1080, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115556056487071744/SP5cJB0C?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1920}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115556056487071744/SP5cJB0C?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 180, "status": 200, "title": "How Do You Measure Flammability?", "unwound_url": "https://www.nist.gov/how-do-you-measure-it/how-do-you-measure-flammability", "url": "https://t.co/toiM5LJ95f"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/BTO1SXjobF", "end": 227, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NIST/status/2115556054075359337/video/1", "media_key": "7_2115555965512638464", "start": 204, "url": "https://t.co/BTO1SXjobF"}]}, "id": "2115556054075359337", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2018, "like_count": 18, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "Flammability describes how easily a material catches fire and how intensely it burns. An instrument called a cone calorimeter can measure these properties.  \n\nLearn more about it: https://t.co/toiM5LJ95f https://t.co/BTO1SXjobF", "url": "https://x.com/NIST/status/2115556054075359337"}, {"author_id": "626660983", "created_at": "2026-10-28T20:43:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115545020040183837"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/fawfulfan/stat…", "end": 282, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/fawfulfan/status/2115402217486168450", "start": 259, "url": "https://t.co/YO0uCLG6WC"}]}, "id": "2115545020040183837", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 7214, "like_count": 270, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 13}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115402217486168450", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I thought this too.\n\nThen I learned that in fact the mom had hired a babysitter to check on the kids regularly and they were only actually home *alone* for a few hours, and had regular adult check-ins.\n\nIdeal situation?\n\nNo.\n\nCriminal arrest of the mom?\n\nNo. https://t.co/YO0uCLG6WC", "url": "https://x.com/lymanstoneky/status/2115545020040183837"}, {"author_id": "626660983", "created_at": "2026-10-28T20:40:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115544170295148951"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/thehill/status…", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/thehill/status/2115514758313255211", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/iMU8WZcmJY"}]}, "id": "2115544170295148951", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 184, "impression_count": 56881, "like_count": 2364, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 85, "retweet_count": 168}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115514758313255211", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "okay but what stood out to me in this story is:\n1) the stunt... worked? they actually got to the point where they could have voted? which seems like a huge problem?\n2) and the state now says that 0.6% of votes, enough to swing elections in some cases, come from the vouching https://t.co/iMU8WZcmJY", "url": "https://x.com/lymanstoneky/status/2115544170295148951"}, {"author_id": "626660983", "created_at": "2026-10-28T20:35:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115542917297393687"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/QualcommPolicy…", "end": 169, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/QualcommPolicy/status/2115461968425566455", "start": 146, "url": "https://t.co/KQ5qxOtmGw"}]}, "id": "2115542917297393687", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1398, "like_count": 19, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115461968425566455", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "cheering for this to work. reshoring a near-complete computer assembly process would be an actual strategic victory for the US, esp. if can scale https://t.co/KQ5qxOtmGw", "url": "https://x.com/lymanstoneky/status/2115542917297393687"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "11348282", "name": "NASA", "username": "NASA"}, {"id": "626660983